  "method_card": {
    "steps": [
      "Write the proportion as an equation with k, e.g. y = kx²",
      "Substitute the known pair to find k",
      "Put k back in, then substitute the new value",
      "Shortcut: y ∝ x² means ×2 on x gives ×4 on y; y ∝ 1/x² means ÷4"
    ],
    "title": "Proportion with Powers",
    "content": "<p>Proportion can involve powers: \\(y \\propto x^2\\) means \\(y = kx^2\\). Similarly \\(y \\propto \\sqrt{x}\\) means \\(y = k\\sqrt{x}\\), and \\(y \\propto \\frac{1}{x^2}\\) means \\(y = \\frac{k}{x^2}\\).</p>",
